G = {}
G['glass-surface-cleaner'] = [
 ('Why ordinary detergents leave streaks','Washing-up liquids and general cleaners contain ingredients that dry as a thin film. On glass, that film scatters light and shows as smears, especially when sunlight falls across a window or a showroom display. A dedicated glass and surface cleaner is formulated to lift dust, fingerprints and light grease and then evaporate cleanly, so the surface dries clear without heavy buffing.'),
 ('Dust, smog and fingerprints','In Lahore and other large cities, fine dust and smog particles settle on glass every day, while doors, counters and touch panels collect fingerprints and skin oils. A good routine removes both: a light spray, a wipe with a clean microfibre cloth, and a final dry pass. Frequent light cleaning takes less time and chemical than occasional heavy cleaning.'),
 ('Surfaces it suits','Besides windows and mirrors, the cleaner is used on glass partitions, display cabinets, stainless steel panels, laminated desks and other smooth, non-porous surfaces. For coated, tinted or specialist glass, test on a small area first and follow the advice given for that surface.'),
 ('Cloths and technique matter','Most streaks come from dirty or fluffy cloths rather than the product. Microfibre cloths, washed without fabric softener and changed often, give the best results. Working from top to bottom and finishing in one direction makes any missed area easy to see.'),
 ('A professional first impression','Reception areas, meeting rooms and showrooms are where clients and auditors form their first view of a company. Clear, clean glass is a small detail that signals a well-run site, and a reliable product makes it easy for housekeeping staff to keep it that way every day.'),
 ('Safe, simple use for staff','The product is used by housekeeping teams with basic protective measures as stated on the label and safety data sheet. Clear dilution and use instructions help new staff get consistent results without guesswork.')]
G['grease-oil-remover'] = [
 ('How emulsification works','Grease and oil do not mix with water, so rinsing alone moves them around rather than removing them. An emulsifying remover breaks oily deposits into tiny droplets surrounded by surfactant, so they can be suspended in water and rinsed away. This makes cleaning faster and leaves parts ready for inspection or reassembly.'),
 ('Where grease builds up','Gearboxes, chains, conveyors, bearings housings, compressor bodies and machine bases all collect grease and dirt over time. That build-up hides cracks and leaks, attracts dust and can become a fire risk near hot surfaces. Regular removal keeps equipment visible, safe and easier to maintain.'),
 ('Soak, brush or spray','Small parts can be soaked in a diluted solution, larger items brushed or sprayed. Allowing a short dwell time lets the product penetrate before rinsing. Warm water often speeds up removal on heavy deposits, where the material allows it.'),
 ('Handling the run-off','Oily rinse water should be collected and handled according to site rules rather than sent straight to storm drains. Seamens can advise on practical handling for your workshop.'),
 ('Protecting cleaned parts','Freshly degreased steel can rust quickly in humid weather. Dry parts promptly and apply lubricant or protective coating before storage or reassembly.'),
 ('Choosing between degreaser grades','For very heavy carbon and oil, the heavy duty degreaser may be more suitable; for routine mechanical parts, the grease and oil remover is often enough. Seamens helps you choose.')]
G['metal-passivator'] = [
 ('Why freshly cleaned metal is vulnerable','Descaling, pickling and degreasing remove scale, rust and oil, but they also leave bare, active metal. In humid air, a fresh steel surface can show flash rust within hours. A passivator treats the cleaned surface so it is less reactive and better protected until it returns to service or receives its final coating.'),
 ('After boiler and heat exchanger cleaning','Chemical cleaning of boilers, condensers and heat exchangers is normally followed by neutralising, rinsing and passivation. This step protects internal surfaces while the equipment is refilled and brought back on line, and helps the water treatment programme start on a clean, stable surface.'),
 ('After fabrication and welding','New tanks, pipework and fabricated parts often carry weld heat tint, mill scale or handling marks. After appropriate cleaning, passivation helps protect the surface. For stainless steel, recognised passivation methods help restore its protective oxide layer.'),
 ('During shutdown and storage','Equipment left idle during long shutdowns or monsoon months can corrode internally. Treating cleaned surfaces before lay-up reduces damage when the plant restarts.'),
 ('Application methods','The passivator can be circulated through closed equipment or applied by spray or immersion for parts. Seamens confirms the method, concentration and contact time for your metal.'),
 ('Checking the result','A uniform, clean surface without fresh rust spots after drying is the first sign of good passivation. For critical work, recognised test methods can be specified.')]
G['drain-pipe-unclogger'] = [
 ('What blocks industrial drains','Drains in kitchens, canteens, washrooms and production areas block with a mixture of grease, soap scum, food waste, fibre and scale. Grease cools and hardens inside pipes, catching other debris until flow slows and finally stops. Chemical clearing breaks down the organic part of the blockage so water can flow again.'),
 ('When chemical clearing makes sense','Chemical unclogging suits slow or partly blocked drains where the cause is organic build-up. Hard objects, collapsed pipes or root intrusion need mechanical methods. If a drain blocks repeatedly in the same place, a camera inspection may show a deeper problem.'),
 ('Safe use','Drain chemicals are strong and must be handled with care. Follow the label, wear gloves and eye protection, never mix with other drain products and keep the area ventilated.'),
 ('Prevention is cheaper','Grease traps, strainers and staff awareness keep most solids out of drains. Regular maintenance doses can keep lines flowing between cleanings.'),
 ('Pipe materials','Pipe materials such as PVC, cast iron and steel are considered before use. Ask Seamens for your system.'),
 ('Reducing downtime','A blocked drain in a production area or kitchen can stop work. Having the right product on site shortens disruption.')]
G['biofilm-remover'] = [
 ('What biofilm is','Biofilm is a slimy layer of bacteria and the material they produce, attached to wet surfaces inside pipes, tanks, cooling systems and process lines. Once established, it protects bacteria from normal disinfectants, harbours organisms that affect hygiene, and can increase corrosion under its layer.'),
 ('Why ordinary disinfection is not enough','Disinfectants added to water often kill free-floating bacteria but cannot reach those protected inside biofilm. A biofilm remover is designed to break down and lift the slime layer so it can be flushed out, after which ongoing treatment is far more effective.'),
 ('Signs of biofilm','Slime on tank walls, rising pressure drop, reduced heat transfer, odours and repeated positive bacteria tests often point to biofilm. Dip slides or swabs help confirm the problem.'),
 ('A clean-then-control approach','After removal, a maintenance programme with suitable biocide treatment and regular flushing stops biofilm returning quickly.'),
 ('Food and process systems','In food and beverage plants, biofilm in water lines and pipework is a hygiene risk. Seamens advises products suitable for each system.'),
 ('Cooling and RO systems','Biofilm in cooling towers and RO plants lowers efficiency and shortens equipment life.')]
G['textile-machine-cleaner'] = [
 ('What builds up on textile machines','Sizing machines collect hardened starch and PVA size, looms gather fly mixed with oil, and stenters build up a sticky mix of finishing chemicals, fibre and oil on chains and frames. These deposits drop onto fabric as stains, increase friction and make inspection harder.'),
 ('Fewer fabric defects','Oil stains and size marks are common causes of seconds in weaving and finishing. Keeping machines clean reduces the chance of deposits transferring to fabric, which protects first-quality output.'),
 ('Cleaning during planned stops','The best time to clean is during scheduled stops, such as beam changes or weekly maintenance. A cleaner that softens deposits quickly shortens that stop.'),
 ('Protecting parts','After cleaning, moving parts should be re-lubricated as per the machine manual.'),
 ('Safer, tidier halls','Clean machines and surrounding floors reduce slips and fire risk from oily fly.'),
 ('Choosing dilution','Seamens advises dilution for each machine and deposit type.')]
G['washroom-cleaner-descaler'] = [
 ('Hard water scale in washrooms','Hard water leaves white or brown scale on toilets, urinals, taps, tiles and shower areas. Scale traps dirt and bacteria, causes odours and makes facilities look neglected even after cleaning. A combined cleaner and descaler removes scale and soil in one step.'),
 ('Odour control starts with scale','Urine scale in urinals and toilet bowls is a common cause of persistent odour. Removing the scale removes the surface where odour-causing bacteria grow.'),
 ('Worker welfare and audits','Clean washrooms matter for staff welfare and are checked during social compliance audits by many international buyers. Well-kept facilities support a good audit result.'),
 ('Routine and deep cleaning','Daily light cleaning and weekly deep descaling keep facilities in good condition with less effort.'),
 ('Surface care','Test on coloured fittings and natural stone, and rinse after use.'),
 ('Safe handling','Use gloves and good ventilation, and never mix with bleach.')]
G['disinfectant-sanitiser'] = [
 ('Clean first, then disinfect','Disinfectants work on clean surfaces. Dirt, grease and food residues shield microorganisms and consume active ingredient. A two-step routine, cleaning then disinfecting, gives reliable hygiene.'),
 ('Contact time is essential','Every disinfectant needs time in contact with the surface. Wiping it off too soon reduces its effect. Follow the stated contact time.'),
 ('Food areas','In food production, sanitising food-contact surfaces is part of the hygiene plan. Seamens advises suitable products and rinsing.'),
 ('Medical and clean rooms','Clinics and clean rooms need regular, documented disinfection.'),
 ('Recognised test standards','Disinfectant performance is tested to recognised European standards for bactericidal activity.'),
 ('Records support audits','Cleaning logs help pass hygiene audits.')]
G['floor-surface-cleaner'] = [
 ('Soils on factory floors','Production floors collect dust, fibre, oil drips, chemical spills and tyre marks. These soils make floors slippery and dull, and spread dirt to products and offices.'),
 ('Slip safety','Oily and dusty floors are a leading cause of slips. Regular cleaning reduces this risk.'),
 ('Manual or machine cleaning','The cleaner suits mopping and scrubber machines; dilution is set for each.'),
 ('Protecting floor finishes','Epoxy and coated floors last longer when cleaned with the right product.'),
 ('Audit ready','Clean floors support buyer audits.')]
